eatening atmosphere about  him which only really becomes apparently  to run in the episode when Cink who  draws our attention to it before that  point tsukasa's performance just fit in  so perfectly without group of pioneers  that it made me really wish that he  would just stay cool and even though I  knew it was coming being a filthy manga  reader and all I found myself really  wanting him to jump on board with the  group although I do have one slight  criticism about Tsukasa and it said I  was a bit disappointed by his animation  in action in the manga Tsukasa is drawn  as this incredible force when he's doing  something like punching a lion or  hunting you can feel the impact of his  raw power leap off the page and smack  you in the face  whereas I didn't quite get that with the  anime and actually as they extended his  whole hunting sequence it very much  struck me as to why that was and for the  most part it's because whenever he  performed in action it would be dealt  with in a static shot for example with  the lion you see him stop throw a punch  then we cut to the result which is a  static shot almost as if we just cut to  the exact page in the manga but with  this impact because it doesn't have the  full force of buoyancy behind it I mean  with all of that sad action isn't  supposed to be the selling point of  doctor stone so I don't really care too  much about not having it be flawless so  long as they nailed the important  character and science stuff and speaking  of what I think this episode did very  effectively would sue castle was convey  his motives in a very relatable and  almost almost reasonable argument in the  marker I found his character change a  bit sudden and mana Loki but in this  episode his flashback was very well  handled with great shots and use of  colour so it made me feel for Tsukasa  which in turn made his ideology much  more appealing to begin with like when  we go to the point where he was rambling  about if we bring everyone back to life  then they'll stop reclaiming the land  charging rent taxes etc I was actually  like look the dude has a point the world  was pretty [ __ ] as it was and it's the  more senior people in power who were  propagating that however then of course  Tsukasa loses me with the whole  purifying Humanity thing and his clear  discrimination against absolutely  everybody above a certain age but still  the anime handled this scene wonderfully  and not just in regards to Tsukasa  either but also sanku in this episode I  think san'ko's deeper character really  got its first chance to shine and one of  those moments was rejecting tsukasa's  ideals and allowing the audience in on  his own personal ambitions which show an  incredible sense of morality for someone  of his intellect in anime I really can't  begin to explain just how refreshing it  is to see someone so smart have such an  idealistic vision of the world because  generally smart characters are in tune  with the world and have become  accustomed to how it works and it'll  take some meat headed idealistic  brute-force protagonists to change their  minds but Senko is there right from the  get-go and I think that's why it becomes  so easy to get on board with him and put  your faith in the sky and during the  episode he also acknowledges that he  would be next to powerless alone and  that he needs the qualities that other  people like tide you can bring to the  rebirth of humanity and this is a theme  that will continue throughout the  entirety of doctor stone and is one of  the reasons why I really love cenk whose  character because as much of an absurd  genius as he is he isn't particularly  arrogant and he also possesses a large  degree of empathy for others who more  stereotypical geniuses would view as  strictly below them but sanku and tide  you pretty much feel like equals which I  really like and thinkers genius was also  highlighted this week in a wonderful  montage about the uses of calcium  carbonate and this was the confirmation  I was looking for to say whether or not  the core concept of this series was  going to be enhanced by the anime there  are an awful lot of points  page after page a scientific exposition  in the manga and I loved every second of  this montage being animated here I don't  think I've ever been so excited for  calcium carbonate in my life but here we  are the way it was portrayed on screen  felt like we were making progress our  first real discovery in regards to human  technological evolution and the sheer  amount of things that such a simple  substance allows them to do it confirmed  to me that the dr. Stearn anime is going  to work that I am going to thoroughly  enjoy this series and to add on to the  list of successes comedy did really well  this week too with my particular  favorite line being usually Hiro doesn't  have a dick and they're really really  like super squishy sounding I poke that  tide you delivered sanku not only that  but I'm also starting to pick up on and  enjoy the general soundtrack of the  series that's an awful lot to the  adventurous atmosphere of Stone Age  science especially the track right at  the beginning of the episode although in  terms of music I will say that after  having seen the ending for first time  I'm I'm not a huge fan of it the song  itself just does nothing for me it feels  frustratingly soft but kind of energetic  at the same time and I just wanted to  pick one either be a soft chilled ending  or an energetic bit of fun like the  opening plus all the shots of the real  world in whatever the hell kind of style  you call that just really put me off  although there is a nice montage of the  characters drawn by Buchi in there and  it is stunning stunning artwork so hey  this ending isn't all bad now I guess  all this left it's point out some  differences with the manga and the main  one this episode was that in the manga  the scene where Tsukasa saves the stone  girl from underneath the rock does not  exist the scene was entirely added to  the anime and I can see why in the short  term it contributes nicely to the idea  of Tsukasa being a good guy but it also  goes on to highlight his greater  philosophy of saving the pure-hearted  young folk and look without any spoilers  it may even go deeper than that so yes  it was a nice addition another thing I  found interesting is that when Cink who  was talking to tied you about Tsukasa he  posited that well what if Tsukasa turns  out to be an evil bureaucrat with  insatiable greed which could not be  further from the truth but in the manga  sync who said something very very  different and wondered what would happen  if Tsukasa turned out to be a sex-crazed  tyrant which mate I'd use little  imagination same with use a hero just a  little bit funnier but that pretty much  does it for episode 2 of doctor stone if  you enjoy this video and the content  this channel produced in general then  please do consider donating to the New  World review patreon because the support  of all the amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share  subscribe because it also helps what  this channels an incredible amount and  if you'd like to join the fun at anytime  then please do head over to my discord  server where a wide array of shenanigan  retakes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts in the episode this has been  the new world review and I'll see you  next time

